declare_clippy_lint! {
    /// ### What it does
    /// Checks for usage of `libc::strlen` on a `CString` or `CStr` value,
    /// and suggest calling `as_bytes().len()` or `to_bytes().len()` respectively instead.
    ///
    /// ### Why is this bad?
